# The companion being played can die, and the protagonist is played in their place.
#
# The sharp edge of the standing death check. A companion is played like the protagonist — it
# observes, thinks and acts for itself — and is therefore the one a failed act's wound penalty lands
# on (see Chapter VI: every gate consults the acting body). So the member played is exactly the
# member the narration can kill, and when it does the map is left with a token nobody answers for.
#
# NarrativeController.SyncRoster answers that: a member no longer in the party is taken off the map
# with their trees, and when they were the one played the protagonist is. This asserts the two
# halves together — the companion is really gone, and the session is still usable afterwards, which
# is what would break if the view were left on somebody dead.
#
# See companion_death_wounds.cli for the notice and the body, which are the same here.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]

# Play the hyena.
click member Brindletail
wait
expect [BRINDLETAIL]

# It takes its turn at the scene — its own observation, thought, act and dice. The goal is pinned:
# the playground's draw over the goals moves whenever an earlier draw does.
strategy succeed
goal smell
click observe "Test Bench"
choose birdsong
advance 12 180
click think "Test Bench"
choose birdsong
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# And is killed by what the narration deals out, being the body that was acting.
wound Brindletail
wait 60

# The notice comes up with nothing clicked, over the narration.
expect Brindletail
expect died of their wounds
click companion-death
wait 60

# Gone from the party...
inspect party
expect-no-state party Brindletail

# ...and a body where they stood.
inspect pois
expect-state pois Brindletail's Remains

# The session survives them: the protagonist is the one played, and the map answers.
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]
click observe way
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element
quit
